WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.610
It is project time! You will bring a favourite object and give your very first one-minute talk.

2
00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:13.690
Pick something you love and can hold up: a toy, a book, a medal, a plant or a drawing.

3
00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:15.700
Choose something with a story.

4
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:21.540
Ask a grown-up before you bring anything special.

5
00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:25.530
Start with a hook so people want to listen.

6
00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:27.920
Ask a question, like have you ever seen a teddy this old?

7
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.560
Or say something surprising.

8
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:35.050
Tell three things about your object.

9
00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:37.990
What it looks like, where it came from, and why it is special to you.

10
00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:40.610
Use describing words and because.

11
00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:45.100
Finish so people know you are done.

12
00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:48.420
Say that is why my teddy is my favourite thing, thank you for listening.

13
00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:51.870
Then smile and wait for the claps.

14
00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:57.010
Listen to Kabir give his show and tell.

15
00:00:57.010 --> 00:01:02.720
Have you ever held a bat that scored fifty runs? This is my lucky cricket bat.

16
00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:10.360
It is light brown, with a red grip. My grandfather gave it to me on my birthday.

17
00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:12.740
It is special because I scored my first fifty with it.

18
00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:16.860
That is why this bat is my favourite thing. Thank you for listening!

19
00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:20.610
Every show and tell follows the same map.

20
00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:25.050
Open with a question or a surprise. Then give three details.

21
00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:29.530
What it looks like, where it came from, and why it is special to you.

22
00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:33.690
Close with, that is why, and thank you for listening.

23
00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:38.450
After each talk, we give two stars and a wish.

24
00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:43.120
A star is something good, like I liked your opening question.

25
00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:48.410
A wish is a kind idea, like next time, could you speak a little louder?

26
00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:51.900
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

27
00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:55.870
Now plan it, build it, test it, and share it!
